WEBVTT

00:03.737 --> 00:06.740
[upbeat music]

00:06.773 --> 00:09.175
[choir vocalizing]

00:09.209 --> 00:11.411
- ♪ We're breaking
new ground ♪

00:11.478 --> 00:13.580
- I'm in Cortland, Ohio,
a small city

00:13.646 --> 00:17.717
60 miles south of Cleveland,
home of the 4-Star Diner,

00:17.784 --> 00:20.887
one of the few establishments
in town that locals depend on

00:20.920 --> 00:22.956
for work and eating out,

00:23.023 --> 00:25.158
run by Gus and his wife, Avgi.

00:25.191 --> 00:27.360
- [speaking Greek]

00:28.995 --> 00:30.130
♪ ♪

00:30.163 --> 00:31.631
- My name is Konstantinos.

00:35.001 --> 00:36.136
But I go with the name Gus.

00:36.169 --> 00:37.871
Even though I don't like it.
[chuckles]

00:37.904 --> 00:40.173
[upbeat jazz music]

00:40.206 --> 00:41.541
- Oh, my god.
What is this?

00:41.608 --> 00:44.511
- Don't [bleep]
bust my balls, man, now.

00:44.544 --> 00:46.246
- My name is Avgi.

00:46.312 --> 00:48.181
- It's 43 years being together.

00:48.214 --> 00:50.116
Now I have to put up
with her, you know.

00:52.485 --> 00:54.387
- Would you like more coffee?

00:54.421 --> 00:56.056
So I decided to come here

00:56.089 --> 00:58.458
because I knew if
I start a business here,

00:58.491 --> 00:59.926
I would have been successful.

00:59.993 --> 01:03.396
I never dreamed that I'm going
to be a restaurant owner.

01:03.463 --> 01:07.300
But I seen that diners was
the future of my business.

01:07.334 --> 01:09.336
American food, good prices,
a cheeseburger,

01:09.369 --> 01:11.304
a hamburger, Italian, Greek.

01:11.338 --> 01:13.506
We been here 15 years.

01:13.573 --> 01:15.608
- What two sides with that
would you like?

01:15.642 --> 01:17.877
- I would describe
4-Star as like--

01:17.944 --> 01:19.079
it's like my second home.

01:19.112 --> 01:20.447
[upbeat rock music]

01:20.513 --> 01:22.415
- Most of our regulars
come almost every day,

01:22.482 --> 01:24.184
three, four times a week.

01:24.250 --> 01:25.251
Here we go.

01:25.285 --> 01:26.519
- That looks really good.

01:26.553 --> 01:28.722
- We're like family
with our customers.

01:31.024 --> 01:31.991
- Um, Gus.

01:32.092 --> 01:33.126
- Gus.
- Gus.

01:33.193 --> 01:34.294
- Gus.
- Let me tell you about Gus.

01:34.361 --> 01:35.795
- [bleep].
Look at this.

01:37.364 --> 01:40.500
[tense dramatic music]

01:40.567 --> 01:42.135
- They're getting
a lot of complaints.

01:43.536 --> 01:44.604
- People are complaining,
but they're customers still.

01:44.738 --> 01:46.373
- That's OK. I don't care.
- How could you just not care?

01:46.439 --> 01:48.141
- I don't give a [bleep]
right now.

01:48.174 --> 01:49.309
- Don't give a crap, then.

01:49.376 --> 01:50.610
Customers hear everything.

01:50.677 --> 01:53.079
They've heard it all
for 15 years.

01:53.113 --> 01:54.714
- We've had customers walk out.

01:54.781 --> 01:56.983
People say that
they'll never come back.

01:56.983 --> 01:59.019
And it's the way
the customers have

01:59.085 --> 02:01.087
seen him treat his employees.

02:01.121 --> 02:02.589
- Your food is coming all raw.

02:02.655 --> 02:04.657
[bleep] [bleep].
And the liver was raw.

02:04.691 --> 02:07.394
The steaks were raw.
[bleep] [bleep].

02:07.427 --> 02:09.229
- It looks like a lot of Greek.

02:09.294 --> 02:10.263
And then you can't
hear anything

02:10.295 --> 02:11.731
except [bleep] [bleep].

02:11.798 --> 02:12.766
[laughs]

02:12.832 --> 02:14.434
♪ ♪

02:14.467 --> 02:15.835
- I don't trust my staff.

02:15.869 --> 02:17.170
Go light on the gravy.

02:17.203 --> 02:18.638
It looks [bleep] gross.

02:18.672 --> 02:20.840
- Maybe if we had a
second to [bleep] breathe.

02:20.907 --> 02:23.376
- We're not going to be able to
do this with you in the window.

02:23.410 --> 02:25.979
I definitely think Gus needs
to trust us to do our job.

02:26.012 --> 02:28.214
Why is Gus standing over in
the corner just watching you?

02:28.281 --> 02:29.482
What do you do wrong?

02:29.549 --> 02:31.317
And they--

02:31.384 --> 02:33.253
- Hey, we're doing
an interview.

02:33.286 --> 02:35.488
Thank you.
Sorry, you gotta go this way.

02:37.490 --> 02:38.425
- [sighs]

02:38.458 --> 02:40.560
[energetic jazz music]

02:40.593 --> 02:42.195
- Hey, Kyle, where's Lexi at?

02:42.262 --> 02:43.396
Where's Lexi at?

02:43.463 --> 02:44.364
- She's in the back
right there.

02:44.431 --> 02:45.632
- This is annoying.

02:45.665 --> 02:48.401
This is the most annoying thing
about this job.

02:48.468 --> 02:50.270
- Lexi, they're going crazy.
What is their complaint?

02:50.337 --> 02:51.338
- This is more stress
than any day

02:51.371 --> 02:52.539
I've ever had here in my life.

02:52.605 --> 02:55.575
- My name's Lexi, and I'm
the head cook of 4-Star Diner.

02:55.608 --> 02:57.711
So I originally came here
as a server.

02:57.777 --> 02:59.646
And they were really
short-staffed in the kitchen,

02:59.713 --> 03:02.182
so I, you know,
helped out one day.

03:02.215 --> 03:03.316
- Still got [bleep].

03:03.316 --> 03:04.484
- I hear you, Gus.

03:04.551 --> 03:06.119
And then I've been stuck
back here ever since.

03:06.186 --> 03:07.354
- It's [bleep].

03:07.387 --> 03:10.523
Before Lexi, we had three
to four people back there.

03:10.623 --> 03:12.158
I didn't trust them at all.

03:12.192 --> 03:15.095
You know,
I fired them on the spot.

03:15.095 --> 03:16.096
Good.

03:16.162 --> 03:18.198
[energetic jazz music]

03:18.231 --> 03:19.332
- Most of my
lessons from cooking

03:19.366 --> 03:20.567
come from watching
cooking TV shows,

03:20.600 --> 03:23.536
so sometimes steak temps are
wrong or egg temps are wrong.

03:23.603 --> 03:24.671
- Here's your guys' salads.
- Thank you.

03:24.738 --> 03:25.839
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

03:25.905 --> 03:27.941
- I trained her everything.

03:28.008 --> 03:29.509
She was like a sponge.

03:29.542 --> 03:31.077
- I've never been trained.

03:31.111 --> 03:32.345
- [sighs]

03:32.379 --> 03:33.380
- Are you OK?

03:33.446 --> 03:34.547
- No, I'm not.
- You're not OK?

03:34.614 --> 03:36.750
- Look at all the plates.
They're not eating their food.

03:36.816 --> 03:39.686
And we keep throwing
food, food, food, food.

03:39.753 --> 03:41.688
With our property,
I have some loans,

03:41.755 --> 03:45.025
and I'll probably
be dead by then,

03:45.091 --> 03:45.992
and I haven't paid them off.

03:46.126 --> 03:49.896
I gotta spend $5,000
to mop up [bleep] [bleep].

03:49.963 --> 03:51.731
- My whole income is my tips.

03:51.798 --> 03:55.669
And if I don't have customers
in here, I'm not paying bills.

03:55.702 --> 03:57.671
What would I do
if this place closed?

03:57.737 --> 03:59.639
- [speaking Greek]

03:59.739 --> 04:02.776
- [speaking Greek]

04:02.842 --> 04:04.511
- This is everything.

04:07.747 --> 04:10.283
[dramatic music]

04:10.316 --> 04:11.851
♪ ♪

04:11.918 --> 04:12.886
- [bleep].

04:12.952 --> 04:13.887
[tense music]

04:13.953 --> 04:16.423
- This restaurant is festering!

04:16.456 --> 04:17.490
You cannot be that deluded!

04:17.524 --> 04:18.692
Stop, stop, stop!

04:18.757 --> 04:20.827
I promise you
you can't do this!

04:20.860 --> 04:21.861
Smell it!

04:21.894 --> 04:22.962
Shut it down!

04:24.564 --> 04:27.901
[upbeat hip-hop music]

04:28.001 --> 04:28.835
♪ ♪

04:28.902 --> 04:31.104
- I am driving through
Cortland, Ohio.

04:31.171 --> 04:35.241
It's a scenic detour about
an hour outside of Cleveland.

04:35.275 --> 04:36.543
Now here as you can see,

04:36.643 --> 04:38.578
it's like a really nice
sense of calm.

04:38.611 --> 04:41.681
It's slow and very,
very beautiful.

04:41.715 --> 04:45.618
Now I'm stopping
by the 4-Star Diner

04:45.685 --> 04:49.689
for what hopefully will be
a really nice, delicious lunch.

04:49.723 --> 04:52.492
Especially after
our long drive.

04:52.559 --> 04:54.094
That's it over there.

04:54.160 --> 04:55.328
♪ ♪

04:55.362 --> 04:57.330
OK, here we are.

04:57.397 --> 04:59.899
Classic American diner.

05:00.433 --> 05:04.437
4-Star Diner,
celebrating 15 years.

05:04.437 --> 05:05.705
Hello.
- Hello.

05:05.739 --> 05:07.440
- Oh, my Lord,
it's busy in here.

05:07.474 --> 05:09.376
- Hello.
- Oh, my god.

05:09.442 --> 05:11.077
Ramsay's here.

05:11.111 --> 05:11.878
Holy crap.

05:12.012 --> 05:14.381
He's sexier in real life
than he is on TV.

05:14.447 --> 05:16.316
- He's here.

05:16.349 --> 05:17.317
You hear me?
- What?

05:17.384 --> 05:18.451
- He's here.
- He's here.

05:18.485 --> 05:20.487
- Oh, my god.
Now I'm nervous.

05:20.587 --> 05:22.288
Um, a little intimidating
having the best chef

05:22.322 --> 05:24.491
in the world in my restaurant.

05:24.557 --> 05:27.227
Oh, my god. He's so awesome.
I can't take it.

05:27.293 --> 05:28.862
- How are you?
- Good. Avgi.

05:28.928 --> 05:30.397
- Avgi. Ah, Gus's wife?

05:30.463 --> 05:31.731
- Yes.
- Lovely.

05:32.799 --> 05:33.667
- Well, well.

05:33.867 --> 05:35.535
- I'd like to go to a seat.
- Yeah.

05:35.602 --> 05:36.770
Shall I sit over there
in the corner?

05:36.836 --> 05:39.105
- Anywhere you like.
- Thank you very much.

05:39.205 --> 05:40.940
Morning.
How are you?

05:41.007 --> 05:42.442
OK.

05:42.509 --> 05:45.512
This is certainly dated,
let me tell you.

05:45.578 --> 05:47.514
It's just a cluster
of knickknacks

05:47.580 --> 05:50.717
and bits of crap
[bleep] everywhere.

05:50.784 --> 05:52.385
As for the deflated balloons,

05:52.452 --> 05:54.921
what a way to celebrate
15 years.

05:54.988 --> 05:56.356
They look so miserable.

05:56.423 --> 05:58.491
Oh, this looks like
the man himself.

05:58.558 --> 05:59.592
Just walked off the catwalk.

05:59.626 --> 06:01.361
- How are you doing, sir?
- Very well, thank you.

06:01.394 --> 06:02.429
How are you?
- Nice.

06:02.495 --> 06:03.663
- We might as well
sit down together.

06:03.730 --> 06:05.365
Are you overdressed
or is it me?

06:05.398 --> 06:06.800
You make me feel all shabby.

06:06.833 --> 06:09.903
Honestly, you're like
an Athens Bee Gee.

06:09.936 --> 06:11.805
- For 20 years,
I was in fashion business.

06:11.871 --> 06:13.506
- Oh, I didn't know that.
- Yes.

06:13.540 --> 06:15.542
- And you're
celebrating 15 years?

06:15.575 --> 06:16.910
- 15 years.
- That's incredible.

06:16.976 --> 06:18.011
Congrats.
- Thank you.

06:18.078 --> 06:19.646
- Well, I'm going to
have a good look around.

06:19.713 --> 06:21.381
I'm going to taste the food.
What would you recommend?

06:21.414 --> 06:23.683
- I recommend the Greek omelet.

06:23.750 --> 06:25.518
- Good. Well,
we'll catch up later, shall we?

06:25.585 --> 06:26.686
- OK, sure.
- Yeah?

06:26.720 --> 06:27.520
- Sure.

06:27.587 --> 06:30.223
[suspenseful percussive music]

06:30.290 --> 06:31.825
♪ ♪

06:31.858 --> 06:33.360
- Good morning.
- How are you?

06:33.393 --> 06:34.160
- I'm doing great.
How are you?

06:34.194 --> 06:35.095
- I'm very well, indeed,
thank you.

06:35.128 --> 06:35.929
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

06:35.995 --> 06:37.897
I'm Karen.
- Karen, good to see you.

06:37.964 --> 06:39.566
- OK.
What are we gonna have today?

06:39.666 --> 06:42.969
- Let's start off with
buffalo chicken strips.

06:43.003 --> 06:46.206
Let's do--I saw a burger.
Route 46, right?

06:46.272 --> 06:48.241
And then let's do the salmon,
please.

06:48.274 --> 06:49.376
Thanks, darling.

06:49.409 --> 06:50.510
Oh, the omelet.

06:50.577 --> 06:51.745
Gus recommended
the Greek omelet.

06:51.778 --> 06:52.712
- The Greek omelet.
OK.

06:52.746 --> 06:55.281
- It's in some authentic
Mediterranean flair.

06:55.348 --> 06:57.150
Yeah.
Thank you very much.

06:57.183 --> 06:58.151
Wow.

06:58.218 --> 06:59.319
- Lexi.

06:59.352 --> 07:00.420
- OK.

07:00.453 --> 07:01.755
- It's Gordon Ramsay's food,
OK?

07:01.788 --> 07:03.023
- OK.

07:03.089 --> 07:03.890
- Do you hear me?
- Yeah.

07:03.990 --> 07:05.959
- No grease, no stuff,
no nothing.

07:05.992 --> 07:08.962
- Kyle, you're going to need
a medium-rare Route 46

07:08.995 --> 07:11.331
as well as the salmon,
all for Ramsay.

07:11.398 --> 07:12.565
I do feel nervous because

07:12.632 --> 07:14.567
he's one of the best chefs
in the world.

07:14.634 --> 07:17.203
I'm an untrained line cook.

07:17.270 --> 07:19.305
I am doing my best.

07:19.372 --> 07:22.208
[suspenseful music]

07:22.275 --> 07:23.243
♪ ♪

07:23.376 --> 07:25.412
- Here's our Greek omelet.
- Oh, the Greek omelet.

07:25.445 --> 07:28.214
OK.
I am excited for this omelet.

07:28.281 --> 07:31.418
[suspenseful music]

07:31.484 --> 07:33.887
♪ ♪

07:33.953 --> 07:35.722
- No seasoning.

07:35.789 --> 07:36.990
Rubber.

07:37.057 --> 07:38.224
Wow.

07:38.291 --> 07:39.626
Not a good start.

07:39.693 --> 07:40.727
- What's wrong with it?

07:40.827 --> 07:43.563
- Oh, no, it's just--
it's just sort of overcooked.

07:43.596 --> 07:45.098
- Overcooked.
I will let her know.

07:45.165 --> 07:46.499
♪ ♪

07:46.533 --> 07:47.734
- Lexi?

07:47.767 --> 07:48.735
- Yes.

07:48.802 --> 07:50.470
- Gordon Ramsay said
your omelet's overcooked.

07:50.503 --> 07:51.905
- Thank you.

07:51.971 --> 07:53.039
It sucks to hear that because
I do take a lot of pride

07:53.139 --> 07:57.243
in my work and try to make
people happy with the food.

07:57.310 --> 08:01.348
♪ ♪

08:01.381 --> 08:02.816
Buffalo strip.

08:02.882 --> 08:04.517
- OK, these are
buffalo chicken strips.

08:04.584 --> 08:07.520
- These are the homemade ones,
right?

08:07.620 --> 08:09.889
What does that mean?
- I don't--[laughs]

08:09.923 --> 08:12.826
- Ask Gus, 'cause
it doesn't smell like it.

08:12.859 --> 08:14.861
- Gus, buffalo chicken tenders.

08:14.894 --> 08:17.197
What part of that's
our own recipe?

08:17.230 --> 08:18.798
- Only our sauce.

08:18.865 --> 08:20.800
- It is not. It is
straight out of the container.

08:20.867 --> 08:21.935
Thank you.

08:23.370 --> 08:26.406
- Wow, they are dry.

08:26.439 --> 08:29.175
- He says only our sauce.

08:29.242 --> 08:30.710
♪ ♪

08:30.777 --> 08:32.479
- And they're frozen, right?

08:32.511 --> 08:33.880
- Yes.

08:33.947 --> 08:36.316
- Yeah, yeah, I'll bypass it.
Thank you, thank you.

08:36.383 --> 08:37.384
- Sorry about that.
- Very strange.

08:37.417 --> 08:38.985
[indistinct chatter]

08:39.052 --> 08:41.453
- Lexi, he said it was dry
and ugh.

08:41.520 --> 08:42.522
- Thank you.

08:42.554 --> 08:44.124
♪ ♪

08:44.190 --> 08:47.527
- Gus is hovering around
like some funeral bearer

08:47.627 --> 08:49.195
waiting for a coffin
to come out.

08:49.262 --> 08:50.063
So uninspiring.

08:50.196 --> 08:53.566
- Everything's available
on the menu today.

08:53.600 --> 08:54.868
- Thank you.
- OK? No, you're welcome.

08:54.934 --> 08:56.136
Gus is putting on a act.

08:56.202 --> 08:59.572
He's trying to be quiet,
not say anything.

08:59.606 --> 09:00.607
And that's not him.

09:00.674 --> 09:01.941
He usually flips out 'cause

09:02.008 --> 09:03.743
the food times
are not coming out

09:03.810 --> 09:05.912
or they're too slow back here
in the kitchen.

09:05.945 --> 09:07.614
I hope
Gordon sees right through him

09:07.647 --> 09:10.150
and that
he's putting on a show.

09:10.216 --> 09:16.556
♪ ♪

09:16.623 --> 09:18.425
- I'll take what's next.

09:18.458 --> 09:20.226
- OK.

09:20.293 --> 09:21.194
♪ ♪

09:22.662 --> 09:23.897
- You ready for your salmon?

09:23.963 --> 09:26.466
- Oh, my god.
How's the salmon cooked?

09:26.533 --> 09:27.567
- On the grill.

09:27.667 --> 09:28.868
- Frozen veg or fresh veg?

09:28.935 --> 09:30.603
- Frozen.
- Frozen.

09:30.670 --> 09:32.605
Thank you.
- You're welcome. Enjoy.

09:32.672 --> 09:36.076
♪ ♪

09:36.142 --> 09:38.345
- Mm.

09:38.411 --> 09:42.148
That tastes disgusting.

09:42.182 --> 09:43.116
And the veg,

09:43.316 --> 09:44.617
it's almost like they've
been cooked in meat juices.

09:44.684 --> 09:47.821
♪ ♪

09:47.854 --> 09:49.989
- You didn't like it?
I saw you spit it out.

09:50.056 --> 09:51.591
- Yeah.
How are they cooking the veg?

09:51.658 --> 09:52.592
What are they doing?

09:52.659 --> 09:54.260
- I really don't know.

09:54.327 --> 09:55.328
- What a mess.

09:55.362 --> 09:56.296
- Thank you.

09:56.429 --> 09:58.598
The salmon was gross
and the veggies were nuked.

09:58.665 --> 10:00.567
So far, he's liked nothing.

10:00.600 --> 10:01.601
- This is not good.

10:01.668 --> 10:03.470
Your Route 46 is going--

10:03.503 --> 10:05.338
- Medium rare.

10:05.405 --> 10:07.507
Here.

10:07.574 --> 10:08.541
- Man, that's quick.

10:08.608 --> 10:09.809
- Enjoy. I'll be back.

10:09.876 --> 10:10.977
- Does it normally
come out this fast?

10:11.077 --> 10:14.214
- It comes up really fast,
pretty much, when Lexi cooks.

10:14.280 --> 10:15.315
- Wow.

10:15.348 --> 10:16.182
- Which isn't very good.

10:16.249 --> 10:17.884
- Does Gus ever
go behind the lines?

10:17.951 --> 10:20.653
- If he does, he's just
a pain in the butt.

10:20.720 --> 10:21.888
- So what does he do here?

10:21.921 --> 10:23.289
- Usually, nothing.

10:23.356 --> 10:24.657
Gets in our way.

10:24.724 --> 10:25.959
He walks as slow as he can.

10:26.026 --> 10:28.261
Let me get you a steak knife.

10:28.361 --> 10:30.497
- Thank you.

10:30.530 --> 10:32.732
So this is the burger.

10:32.766 --> 10:36.302
This smells a little bit weird.

10:36.369 --> 10:38.605
♪ ♪

10:38.638 --> 10:40.640
[sniffs]

10:40.707 --> 10:43.410
♪ ♪

10:43.476 --> 10:44.377
Damn.

10:44.444 --> 10:46.646
You have something that
is not right in there.

10:46.713 --> 10:48.515
And I do not know what that is.

10:48.581 --> 10:49.783
- So?

10:49.816 --> 10:52.052
- Yeah, just--
something smells in there.

10:52.118 --> 10:53.987
Is everything clean and fresh?

10:54.054 --> 10:56.489
Is it--do they cook fresh?

10:56.523 --> 10:57.691
- Yeah.

10:58.725 --> 10:59.826
- Yeah. Mm.

10:59.859 --> 11:03.029
ry[dramatic music]

11:03.096 --> 11:05.298
♪ ♪

11:05.365 --> 11:06.433
- Yeah--ooh.

11:06.466 --> 11:07.367
- Everything OK here?

11:07.467 --> 11:09.069
- Yeah, I've had better days,
but all good.

11:09.135 --> 11:10.804
How are you?
- I don't know.

11:10.837 --> 11:12.138
- You don't know.

11:12.205 --> 11:14.941
- If you don't know how
you are, then I'm [bleep].

11:15.041 --> 11:17.744
- I'm going to sit down.
- What's happened?

11:17.811 --> 11:20.246
Why is it failing?
What is happening?

11:20.313 --> 11:21.314
I'm sorry.

11:21.381 --> 11:22.615
Are you OK?

11:22.682 --> 11:25.118
I'm sorry.
I'm sorry.

11:25.151 --> 11:29.055
But what are the problems
in the restaurant?

11:37.397 --> 11:39.966
[somber music]

11:40.033 --> 11:42.969
- Are you OK?
- Yeah. I--

11:43.003 --> 11:45.171
[sniffles]
- I'm here to help, OK?

11:45.271 --> 11:47.007
And I'll talk
to all of you after.

11:48.008 --> 11:50.710
- Thank you, Avgi.
Thank you.

11:50.777 --> 11:52.679
- [sniffles]
- [sighs] Ooh.

11:52.712 --> 11:56.416
♪ ♪

11:56.483 --> 11:58.151
[tense music]

11:58.218 --> 12:00.053
- Thank you very much.
Thank you.

12:00.086 --> 12:03.390
♪ ♪

12:03.456 --> 12:06.459
- Let's get--
let's get the entire team out.

12:06.526 --> 12:08.528
- Everybody out front.

12:08.595 --> 12:10.030
- Let's go.

12:10.096 --> 12:11.564
♪ ♪

12:11.598 --> 12:15.268
Listen, I'll be honest.

12:15.301 --> 12:19.739
The whole experience
was just sad.

12:19.773 --> 12:21.641
Gus, this was your dream?

12:21.708 --> 12:23.677
- Yes, it was, and it still is.

12:23.743 --> 12:26.613
- And it still is?
- Yes.

12:26.646 --> 12:27.647
- Let's talk about the food.

12:27.714 --> 12:29.015
It's called 4-Star Diner.

12:29.049 --> 12:31.418
One star, one star, one star.

12:31.484 --> 12:33.053
♪ ♪

12:33.153 --> 12:35.555
Gus, are you proud
of this place?

12:35.622 --> 12:36.456
- Yes, I am.

12:36.623 --> 12:39.526
- What are you proud of?
'Cause I'm struggling.

12:39.592 --> 12:40.827
- Uh--

12:40.894 --> 12:43.730
- Wow.
Feels like we've given up.

12:43.763 --> 12:45.398
- That's exactly how it feels.

12:46.966 --> 12:49.302
- Gus, talk to me.

12:50.637 --> 12:53.073
I have to repeat myself
over and over.

12:53.139 --> 12:54.674
And don't do this,
don't do this,

12:54.774 --> 12:55.975
don't do this, don't do this.

12:56.042 --> 12:58.511
- So your staff
aren't listening to you?

12:58.545 --> 13:00.113
- Yes.

13:00.180 --> 13:01.548
- So it's a staffing issue?

13:01.614 --> 13:05.051
- The simplest thing,
I have to tell them ten times.

13:05.118 --> 13:06.886
- You don't
appreciate us at all.

13:06.920 --> 13:08.722
- I do appreciate them.

13:08.788 --> 13:09.823
Maybe they're not feeling it.

13:09.889 --> 13:11.224
- We're not feeling it.

13:11.291 --> 13:13.927
- Maybe because I don't go
around every day and saying,

13:13.993 --> 13:15.829
oh, you're doing this.
oh, thank you.

13:15.895 --> 13:17.364
Or--yes.

13:17.397 --> 13:20.667
- You know how much better
we'd do if you did that for us?

13:20.734 --> 13:22.569
- But are you encouraging them?

13:22.569 --> 13:23.370
- No.
- No.

13:23.370 --> 13:24.537
- You're not
encouraging the team?

13:24.604 --> 13:26.006
- No.

13:26.072 --> 13:27.674
- So you believe it's good food
and good service?

13:27.707 --> 13:29.442
- Yes.

13:29.509 --> 13:30.944
Strongly.

13:30.977 --> 13:32.912
[dramatic music]

13:32.979 --> 13:34.447
- You can't see any problem
in here?

13:36.850 --> 13:37.817
Definitely.

13:37.851 --> 13:38.852
- [chuckling] Yeah.

13:38.918 --> 13:41.421
- Oh, my goodness me.
Wow.

13:46.860 --> 13:48.595
[tense music]

13:48.661 --> 13:50.897
- Gus, are you proud
of this place?

13:50.964 --> 13:52.132
- Yes, I am.

13:52.232 --> 13:53.800
- What are you proud of?
'Cause I'm struggling.

13:53.833 --> 13:54.868
- Uh--

13:54.934 --> 13:56.636
- You don't appreciate us
at all.

13:56.703 --> 13:57.504
- Wow.

13:57.704 --> 13:59.839
- Chef, how many times
can you repeat yourself?

13:59.873 --> 14:02.842
- So your staff aren't
listening to you?

14:02.876 --> 14:04.511
- Yes.

14:04.544 --> 14:07.180
- But the only person not
doing anything today was you.

14:07.247 --> 14:09.416
All I could see was this man
just standing there like that.

14:09.482 --> 14:13.153
I'm like, is he actually
going to do anything?

14:13.219 --> 14:14.587
- Do I do help you out?
- You saw it.

14:14.654 --> 14:15.755
- No.

14:15.889 --> 14:17.357
- Well, when you're in our way
thinking you're helping out,

14:17.390 --> 14:20.160
you're not really helping,
but you think you are.

14:20.226 --> 14:21.761
It's pretty much bullcrap what
Gus was doing,

14:21.828 --> 14:25.298
blaming us for everything when
he does nothing around here.

14:25.365 --> 14:29.102
He don't take any of the blame
and then we feel all degraded.

14:29.135 --> 14:31.104
- OK, an owner
that's in denial.

14:31.137 --> 14:33.406
Can I have a word
with the front of house?

14:33.506 --> 14:34.441
- Sure.

14:34.607 --> 14:35.842
- Do you want to grab
some fresh air and a coffee

14:35.875 --> 14:38.645
and--oh, my Lord.

14:38.712 --> 14:40.880
Dear, oh, dear, oh, dear.

14:40.914 --> 14:42.215
What is really going on?

14:42.282 --> 14:44.084
- We're flying by the seats
of our pants every day.

14:44.150 --> 14:45.819
- Gus does tell us
to say that the food

14:45.885 --> 14:47.420
is fresh and not frozen.

14:47.487 --> 14:48.555
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

14:48.655 --> 14:51.758
He told me to tell you the
buffalo sauce was homemade.

14:51.791 --> 14:53.460
- Oh, my goodness me, this guy.

14:53.526 --> 14:55.228
Is he on his best behavior
right now?

14:55.261 --> 14:56.463
- Yes.
- 'Cause I'm in the building?

14:56.496 --> 14:57.630
all: Yes.

14:57.764 --> 14:59.432
- How does he normally perform
when I'm not here, truthfully?

14:59.466 --> 15:01.067
- He will yell.
He'll yell and scream at you.

15:01.101 --> 15:03.069
- And this is
in front of customers?

15:03.103 --> 15:05.205
- Oh, yes. Definitely.
- Wow.

15:05.271 --> 15:07.607
OK, can you just show me how
this place functions tonight

15:07.640 --> 15:10.276
and let me have a good look
at how this system works?

15:10.310 --> 15:11.378
- OK.
- Thank you so much.

15:11.444 --> 15:12.212
- We appreciate it.
- Oh, my gosh.

15:12.312 --> 15:14.414
So glad you're here.
- We can breathe?

15:14.514 --> 15:16.082
- Yeah.
Thanks, Chef.

15:16.149 --> 15:17.450
- Well, let's get
one thing clear.

15:17.484 --> 15:19.219
That is not
a four-star performance.

15:19.285 --> 15:21.488
The food is--
it's not even one star.

15:21.521 --> 15:23.590
And there's something going on
a little bit deeper

15:23.623 --> 15:26.459
and I need to get
to the bottom of this quickly.

15:26.526 --> 15:27.927
[suspenseful music]

15:27.961 --> 15:31.097
[upbeat percussive music]

15:31.164 --> 15:32.799
- Everybody ready
to do their job?

15:32.866 --> 15:33.933
- Yep.

15:33.967 --> 15:35.035
- Going into service tonight,

15:35.101 --> 15:36.236
Gus needs
to get his act together

15:36.236 --> 15:38.204
and show how he really is

15:38.271 --> 15:40.407
and not walk on eggshells
because Ramsay's here.

15:40.473 --> 15:42.409
- Hi. How are you?
- Good. How are you?

15:42.475 --> 15:44.277
- Customers coming in.
About to get to showtime.

15:44.344 --> 15:46.179
- How's everybody doing?
- Good.

15:46.212 --> 15:47.313
- Mile-high turkey dinner.

15:47.347 --> 15:48.481
- Just a waffle?
- Yeah.

15:48.515 --> 15:49.883
- Mashed potatoes,
gravy on everything.

15:49.949 --> 15:51.685
- Meat and cheese only
on that Philly, please.

15:51.718 --> 15:52.719
- Perfect.

15:52.786 --> 15:53.720
- Thank you.

15:53.920 --> 15:56.389
- First order, short stack,
full stack French toast.

15:56.423 --> 15:58.758
- OK. If I wasn't here,
what would you do?

15:59.793 --> 16:00.827
- Please don't stop.

16:01.127 --> 16:02.562
- Don't stop.

16:04.564 --> 16:05.699
- OK.

16:06.232 --> 16:08.168
- I tell you what is good
is our roast pork loin.

16:08.234 --> 16:10.136
We make that homemade in-house.

16:10.203 --> 16:11.204
- Lexi?
- Yeah.

16:11.271 --> 16:14.407
- Make sure he doesn't
give no raw food out today.

16:14.474 --> 16:17.143
- Thank god Gus is here
to tell us how to work.

16:17.177 --> 16:18.578
- Thank god for that.

16:18.678 --> 16:20.547
- It is tough having Gordon
Ramsay in here evaluating,

16:20.647 --> 16:22.615
but I definitely am
looking forward to it.

16:22.682 --> 16:24.284
I think it's going
to be for the better,

16:24.351 --> 16:26.519
so very excited to have him
in here critiquing everything.

16:28.088 --> 16:29.989
- Give me an insight
to how this works.

16:30.023 --> 16:31.057
How do you organize the line?

16:31.124 --> 16:33.493
- Fried and egg grill,
I usually run.

16:33.593 --> 16:34.527
- Right.

16:34.661 --> 16:36.129
- He runs main grill,
which is burgers, chicken.

16:36.162 --> 16:37.597
- Right.
- Grilled cheese, home fries.

16:37.630 --> 16:38.465
- Gotcha.

16:38.531 --> 16:40.166
- Medium-rare
on that steak, Hal.

16:40.266 --> 16:42.135
We're gonna pull it off.

16:42.168 --> 16:43.403
- And how do you
section this off?

16:43.470 --> 16:45.438
What goes where?

16:45.472 --> 16:47.741
- I mean, really, however.
Room.

16:47.807 --> 16:48.842
- No?

16:49.009 --> 16:50.477
So there's no organization?
You just throw it on there?

16:50.510 --> 16:51.745
- Right.
- Wow.

16:51.811 --> 16:55.281
♪ ♪

16:55.315 --> 16:56.316
- Hi, guys.
How are you?

16:56.316 --> 16:59.185
- How are you?
- Good. Two?

16:59.252 --> 17:00.887
- Yes.
- OK.

17:00.920 --> 17:03.123
Medium-rare, mashed potatoes.

17:03.189 --> 17:04.089
- Can I ask if you
have a check down there

17:04.156 --> 17:05.525
for a sirloin steak sandwich?

17:05.592 --> 17:07.160
It's been a while, long while.
- Yeah, right here.

17:07.227 --> 17:09.061
It's the one we're
working on now.

17:11.330 --> 17:12.799
- Shouldn't
be too much longer now.

17:12.866 --> 17:13.900
- OK.

17:14.166 --> 17:15.300
- Is that cold?

17:15.535 --> 17:17.604
- You want me to
take them back, guys?

17:17.671 --> 17:18.605
- No.

17:19.005 --> 17:20.006
- You sure?

17:20.040 --> 17:21.141
- I'm so sorry.

17:21.174 --> 17:24.778
[dramatic music]

17:24.844 --> 17:26.046
♪ ♪

17:26.079 --> 17:27.079
- The steak is--mm.

17:27.180 --> 17:28.615
it's very chewy.

17:28.682 --> 17:29.783
- OK.

17:33.286 --> 17:35.321
- Hey, guys,
we got a send-back.

17:35.388 --> 17:36.890
- Oh.

17:36.956 --> 17:39.592
To be honest, I think
this dinner service is a joke.

17:39.626 --> 17:42.195
I think the pressure
is just on having Gordon here.

17:42.228 --> 17:44.064
Tink everybody's feeling
a little bit nervous

17:44.097 --> 17:45.865
and making
a little bit of mistakes.

17:45.932 --> 17:47.367
- Everything good?

17:49.402 --> 17:51.338
- Let me take it
back for you, hon.

17:51.404 --> 17:53.273
♪ ♪

17:53.340 --> 17:54.407
- What did they say is wrong?

17:54.441 --> 17:56.976
- They just say texture
and everything looks gross.

17:57.010 --> 17:58.878
- Is it frozen?

17:58.945 --> 17:59.946
- No.

17:59.979 --> 18:01.181
- It's not frozen?
- No.

18:01.247 --> 18:03.216
Then why are they defrosting on
the top of the oven over there?

18:03.316 --> 18:04.884
- It was frozen.
It is thawed now.

18:04.951 --> 18:06.219
- He's just lying.

18:06.252 --> 18:08.421
I know, but he's just
lying to me.

18:08.488 --> 18:10.256
- No, maybe I don't
understand your question.

18:10.323 --> 18:12.258
- Is this product frozen?

18:12.325 --> 18:13.360
- They come frozen
and we cut 'em up.

18:13.393 --> 18:14.761
- So that means yes.
- Yes.

18:14.828 --> 18:16.029
- Right.
OK.

18:16.096 --> 18:17.630
Thank you.
Frozen.

18:17.664 --> 18:19.933
- I think Gus just has
a problem admitting his wrongs.

18:19.966 --> 18:22.469
I think he's just
so used to lying to everybody.

18:22.502 --> 18:24.270
I mean, to lie
to Gordon Ramsay,

18:24.337 --> 18:26.006
to lie to anybody
about it being fresh,

18:26.072 --> 18:27.207
it's just not right.

18:29.242 --> 18:31.611
- All right.

18:31.678 --> 18:34.381
Lexi, are you ready
for this shrimp?

18:34.414 --> 18:35.615
- Yes. There's three orders.
Just plate them.

18:35.682 --> 18:37.150
- You want me to separate it
and what?

18:37.217 --> 18:39.619
- Yeah.
He's killing me.

18:39.686 --> 18:41.054
- He's in the kitchen now
with an apron on.

18:41.121 --> 18:41.988
Is that normal?
Because I'm here?

18:42.055 --> 18:42.989
- No.
- No.

18:43.023 --> 18:44.224
- No.

18:44.290 --> 18:45.125
- What is he doing?
He's on the grill now.

18:45.191 --> 18:46.159
- He's gonna be in the way.

18:46.292 --> 18:47.627
- And again, do you think
that's because I'm here?

18:47.694 --> 18:48.895
- Yes.
- Wow.

18:48.962 --> 18:49.963
- Where's my olives at?

18:49.996 --> 18:50.964
- They're in the cooler.

18:50.997 --> 18:52.899
- He doesn't know how
to finish these things?

18:52.966 --> 18:53.733
- He's never been back here.

18:53.833 --> 18:54.734
- He's never been back here?
- Ever.

18:54.901 --> 18:56.236
- I think Gus is acting
a little different today.

18:56.302 --> 18:57.437
I think he's a little nervous

18:57.437 --> 18:58.538
to show everybody
his true colors.

18:58.605 --> 19:02.108
- How's my gyro?
Where's my gyro?

19:02.175 --> 19:04.544
- 4-Star Diner it isn't,
let me tell you.

19:04.577 --> 19:06.579
The big issue
I've got right now is Gus.

19:06.613 --> 19:07.847
He's faking it.

19:07.881 --> 19:10.250
And he's going around putting
band-aids on everybody.

19:10.283 --> 19:13.653
This guy is full of [bleep].

19:13.753 --> 19:14.454
Uh, Gus.

19:14.587 --> 19:15.522
- We're gonna get you
some lunch.

19:15.588 --> 19:16.823
- Two seconds?

19:16.890 --> 19:19.526
[tense music]

19:19.626 --> 19:20.694
♪ ♪

19:20.727 --> 19:22.996
What are you doing?
Are you faking it?

19:23.029 --> 19:24.531
- I'm not faking [bleep].

19:24.597 --> 19:26.533
- I'm going to call you out.
You are.

19:26.599 --> 19:27.567
You never go behind the line.

19:27.667 --> 19:29.703
You're jumping in,
you're grabbing bits of food.

19:29.769 --> 19:31.338
It's just--I've never
seen anything like this.

19:31.404 --> 19:34.307
- 100%, I give you
my word as a man.

19:34.341 --> 19:36.209
- Right.
- This is not a fake. Trust me.

19:36.276 --> 19:37.344
- I'm just asking
because everyone's

19:37.377 --> 19:38.978
saying this is not normal.

19:39.079 --> 19:40.447
And I don't trust you.

19:40.513 --> 19:42.916
I've got to be honest with you.
I don't trust you.

19:43.016 --> 19:43.850
I smell a rat.

19:43.950 --> 19:45.318
- What do I have--
what do I have to do?

19:45.352 --> 19:46.453
- I'm just asking you.

19:46.486 --> 19:47.687
- No, no, no
- Is this real?

19:47.754 --> 19:48.588
- It's not fake at all.

19:48.688 --> 19:50.256
- Show me how
you run your business.

19:50.323 --> 19:52.492
- Right.
That's what I'm doing.

19:55.061 --> 19:56.896
- Ugh.

19:56.963 --> 19:57.797
- So gross.

19:57.964 --> 19:59.866
How many times a week
is this kitchen cleaned?

19:59.933 --> 20:00.700
- Deep clean?

20:00.767 --> 20:02.002
None. No times a week.

20:02.035 --> 20:03.269
- Disgusting.

20:03.336 --> 20:05.438
- I wish the cleanliness
was different.

20:05.505 --> 20:06.639
I've been trying
to do what I can,

20:06.673 --> 20:08.541
but Gus did not train me
at all.

20:08.608 --> 20:12.946
- Gus, when was the last time
this kitchen was deep-cleaned?

20:13.947 --> 20:16.883
- Every single night?
- Yeah.

20:16.950 --> 20:19.853
[dramatic music]

20:19.919 --> 20:26.326
♪ ♪

20:28.795 --> 20:31.431
- Right.
Fridge time.

20:31.498 --> 20:34.734
Oh, my goodness me.
Look at the state of that.

20:34.801 --> 20:39.506
Bloody hell.
Raw meat sat with cooked meat.

20:40.540 --> 20:42.909
[coughs] Ground burger.

20:42.976 --> 20:45.245
Oh, my god.

20:45.278 --> 20:46.780
Lexi, stop cooking.

20:46.846 --> 20:47.447
- Done.

20:47.514 --> 20:49.349
[dramatic music]

20:49.416 --> 20:50.784
- Gus, come here.

20:50.850 --> 20:53.653
Ladies and gentlemen,
I need to stop you from eating.

20:53.687 --> 20:56.623
I hate to be the bearer
of bad news,

20:56.656 --> 20:59.659
but I was hoping that you were
going to somewhat have at least

20:59.693 --> 21:02.729
a sort of two-
or three-star dinner tonight.

21:02.796 --> 21:05.899
Did someone have
the burger tonight?

21:05.965 --> 21:08.268
- My table did,
but did not receive it yet.

21:08.301 --> 21:14.007
♪ ♪

21:14.040 --> 21:17.344
- Just smell them.

21:17.410 --> 21:19.245
Just smell them.

21:19.279 --> 21:22.248
♪ ♪

21:22.282 --> 21:23.483
That's not fresh.

21:23.550 --> 21:25.185
- I've been trying
to get a date gun

21:25.251 --> 21:26.553
since I started
in this kitchen.

21:26.586 --> 21:27.854
They're just,
you know, not hearing me.

21:27.921 --> 21:29.289
If the health inspector
comes in here--

21:29.389 --> 21:30.490
If anybody comes in here,

21:30.557 --> 21:32.826
you don't know
if it's old, if it's fresh.

21:32.859 --> 21:34.728
- Forget about that [bleep]
and throw it away.

21:34.794 --> 21:37.464
- What did you just say?
Forget about that [bleep]?

21:37.530 --> 21:39.366
- Throw it away.
- How dare you?

21:39.432 --> 21:41.267
- How dare me?
- Can you smell that?

21:41.334 --> 21:42.435
- Yes.

21:42.502 --> 21:45.939
- I am very shocked that Gus
would just not care enough

21:46.006 --> 21:48.541
to make sure that
all of our products are fresh

21:48.575 --> 21:50.577
and not going
to get anyone sick.

21:50.643 --> 21:53.313
- You gentlemen,
OK, how many years

21:53.380 --> 21:54.781
have you been coming here?

21:54.848 --> 21:58.084
Do you ever have a [bleep]
hamburger that smelled?

21:59.652 --> 22:01.821
- OK. Did you think that
I did that purposely?

22:01.855 --> 22:02.989
- This is not yours?

22:03.023 --> 22:06.593
- I'm not responsible to
check every [bleep] letter.

22:06.626 --> 22:08.762
Guys, I'm really sorry, OK?

22:08.795 --> 22:11.631
You don't have to eat it.
You don't have to pay.

22:11.698 --> 22:13.166
- Oh, thank you for that.
You don't have to eat it.

22:13.199 --> 22:14.367
- You don't have to do [bleep].

22:14.401 --> 22:17.203
Please do not come back!

22:17.270 --> 22:19.873
I'm done.
- What?

22:25.345 --> 22:26.746
[dramatic music]

22:26.780 --> 22:30.750
- You don't have to eat it.
You don't have to pay.

22:30.817 --> 22:31.985
- Oh, thank you for that.
You don't have to eat it.

22:32.052 --> 22:33.053
- You don't have to do [bleep].

22:33.086 --> 22:34.721
- I think he's going
to see the real Gus.

22:34.788 --> 22:38.191
I think that Gus is gonna
start ripping us a new one.

22:38.224 --> 22:40.894
- Please do not come back!

22:40.960 --> 22:44.597
I'm done.
- What?

22:44.664 --> 22:47.067
Please go home,
ladies and gentlemen.

22:47.100 --> 22:48.335
♪ ♪

22:48.368 --> 22:50.503
- Thank you guys
for everything, OK?

22:50.537 --> 22:51.504
- So sorry, guys.

22:51.538 --> 22:52.605
Oh, my god.

22:52.672 --> 22:57.811
Our shot at fixing this
restaurant is possibly over.

22:57.877 --> 23:00.180
- What if nobody
ever comes back?

23:00.280 --> 23:01.781
Like, what if
we really do shut down?

23:01.815 --> 23:04.484
I'm not prepared
to be out of work.

23:04.517 --> 23:06.019
- I don't want you
to be prepared.

23:06.086 --> 23:07.520
But right now, I'm banging
my head against the wall

23:07.587 --> 23:09.189
with this guy.
He is not listening.

23:09.222 --> 23:11.825
First, it's your--the staff,
the team not listening.

23:11.858 --> 23:14.661
Now it's the customers.
This guy's deluded.

23:14.694 --> 23:15.829
Where is he?
- I don't know.

23:15.862 --> 23:16.629
Probably ran off.
- Where is he?

23:16.730 --> 23:19.599
I need some time with him
on my own.

23:19.699 --> 23:21.434
- You know how sad it is
to stand out there

23:21.501 --> 23:23.503
and watch him give excuses
like that for us

23:23.536 --> 23:25.271
and put that [bleep] on us?
- Yep.

23:25.305 --> 23:26.406
- Like it's our [bleep] fault?

23:26.439 --> 23:29.376
♪ ♪

23:29.409 --> 23:32.479
- What is wrong with you?

23:32.545 --> 23:34.214
- Like, about what?

23:34.280 --> 23:36.716
[tense music]

23:36.783 --> 23:38.051
♪ ♪

23:38.118 --> 23:41.621
- You're taking advantage
of your customers.

23:41.688 --> 23:44.724
You're taking advantage
of this town.

23:44.791 --> 23:48.762
And you know what?
Your staff, they're petrified.

23:48.828 --> 23:52.632
You show no respect
to the staff.

23:52.699 --> 23:56.002
I need you to wake up.

23:56.069 --> 23:56.870
- [sighs]

23:56.903 --> 23:57.704
- 'Cause ever since
I met you,

23:57.771 --> 24:00.540
all it is is just
excuse after excuse.

24:00.573 --> 24:02.208
You are the problem here.

24:02.242 --> 24:06.246
- [groans] Chef, to be honest,
I don't agree with you.

24:06.312 --> 24:08.148
- Game over, Gus.

24:08.181 --> 24:09.582
- Game over?

24:09.616 --> 24:11.618
The game is never over with me.

24:11.651 --> 24:12.752
Game just started.

24:12.819 --> 24:14.988
- Nah, I'm done
with that [bleep].

24:15.021 --> 24:18.491
And I'm not gonna hang around
with my team to change you.

24:18.525 --> 24:21.594
And the only way
I'd consider staying

24:21.628 --> 24:24.197
is if you get in
every member of your staff

24:24.264 --> 24:25.832
and apologize to them.

24:25.899 --> 24:27.133
♪ ♪

24:27.167 --> 24:30.437
If you're not gonna do that,
then I can't help you.

24:30.503 --> 24:32.472
I'm leaving.

24:32.472 --> 24:39.813
♪ ♪

24:43.216 --> 24:45.652
I am done.

24:45.685 --> 24:47.053
- Where is Gordon?

24:47.120 --> 24:48.254
Do you know where he went?

24:48.321 --> 24:49.289
- Gordon left.

24:49.356 --> 24:50.490
He took off.

24:50.557 --> 24:52.225
- Oh, lordy.

24:52.292 --> 24:53.560
♪ ♪

24:53.626 --> 24:55.061
- I can't stay here
and hang around

24:55.128 --> 24:57.664
if that guy's
not prepared to change.

24:57.697 --> 24:59.432
Trading on 15 years'
reputation,

24:59.466 --> 25:03.636
that's been failing--this guy
needs to show some humility.

25:03.670 --> 25:06.639
He needs to start
apologizing for what he's done

25:06.706 --> 25:10.243
to that loyal team
before it's too late.

25:10.276 --> 25:12.579
♪ ♪

25:12.645 --> 25:14.514
[indistinct chatter]

25:14.581 --> 25:16.282
- Hey, what's going on?

25:16.783 --> 25:18.551
- Nice to meet you.

25:23.823 --> 25:26.793
[suspenseful music]

25:26.893 --> 25:28.995
♪ ♪

25:31.598 --> 25:32.932
- What's that?

25:35.769 --> 25:38.371
- When you guys don't have
this diner,

25:38.438 --> 25:40.907
you're gonna be sorry.

25:45.812 --> 25:47.981
- Gordon can't help us if
he is not gonna help himself.

25:48.081 --> 25:49.649
- Do you really think
Gus is gonna own up

25:49.683 --> 25:52.318
to any of what
he showed tonight?

25:52.352 --> 25:55.488
- I'm going to use his words.
This is all [bleep].

25:55.555 --> 25:57.323
- Well, it was nice
knowing you all.

25:57.390 --> 25:58.224
- Hey.

25:58.291 --> 25:59.392
- Stop it.
- Yeah, right.

25:59.426 --> 26:01.995
- He came in here one day,

26:02.028 --> 26:04.998
one [bleep] day,
and he said he ain't coming--

26:05.065 --> 26:08.101
I don't want [bleep]
back in here anyway!

26:08.168 --> 26:09.002
- OK.

26:09.202 --> 26:11.871
- How he [bleep] judge me
in one [bleep] hour?

26:11.905 --> 26:13.340
- Gus is back there screaming.

26:13.406 --> 26:14.474
- We're gonna close.

26:14.574 --> 26:15.975
- [bleep] him!

26:16.042 --> 26:17.877
I don't want--

26:17.944 --> 26:18.978
anyway!

26:19.045 --> 26:20.980
Tell him to get
the [bleep] out of here!

26:21.014 --> 26:22.749
You think I need his [bleep]?

26:22.782 --> 26:25.518
Do you think I need [bleep]?

26:25.585 --> 26:26.853
15 [bleep] years!

26:26.920 --> 26:28.655
- No.
- I don't give a [bleep]!

26:28.688 --> 26:30.690
All right!
Get the [bleep] out of here!

26:30.724 --> 26:32.592
Get the [bleep] out of here!

26:32.625 --> 26:34.394
- Oh, my goodness.

26:34.461 --> 26:35.662
[dramatic music]

26:35.729 --> 26:36.930
- Guys, guys get
the [bleep] out of here.

26:36.996 --> 26:38.264
You're all--
- What happened now?

26:38.298 --> 26:40.433
- He left. He ain't
coming back here no more.

26:40.500 --> 26:43.103
- That's because you're not
taking accountability, Gus.

26:43.169 --> 26:45.138
- [bleep] him and
[bleep] all of you.

26:45.171 --> 26:46.639
- No. You [bleep] apologize.
- Get the [bleep] out of here.

26:46.740 --> 26:48.575
- You have to just
take accountability, Gus!

26:48.608 --> 26:49.809
- What you--
- What? In one hour?

26:49.876 --> 26:50.844
- Because we're all
going to walk!

26:50.944 --> 26:52.545
- In one [bleep] hour?
- What are you going to do?

26:52.645 --> 26:54.647
[Gus screaming indistinctly]

26:54.714 --> 26:55.815
You, two hours, like a puppy!

26:55.882 --> 26:56.950
- Right, you have
to apologize to us,

26:57.083 --> 26:58.918
- In one hour! In one hour!
- That's the whole problem.

26:58.985 --> 27:00.120
- He wasn't here to apologize!

27:00.153 --> 27:01.821
- Not him.
You apologize to us.

27:01.888 --> 27:02.989
- You need to try!

27:03.023 --> 27:03.990
- [bleep]
I can't [bleep] right now.

27:04.024 --> 27:05.658
- So what, we're just done?

27:05.725 --> 27:08.628
[tense music]

27:08.661 --> 27:10.430
♪ ♪

27:10.497 --> 27:12.999
- Give me a second.

27:13.066 --> 27:15.535
♪ ♪

27:15.568 --> 27:17.003
- What are we gonna do?

27:17.070 --> 27:19.606
- No job?
Are you kidding me?

27:19.639 --> 27:20.840
- I don't understand.

27:20.940 --> 27:23.443
- You don't understand?
Ask your [bleep] husband.

27:23.510 --> 27:25.278
- [bleep].

27:25.311 --> 27:28.982
- It's just really upsetting
that Gus would act like this

27:29.049 --> 27:32.218
and not take accountability
that this is his restaurant.

27:32.285 --> 27:33.853
- Look, everybody's
taking their cameras.

27:33.920 --> 27:35.689
They're all leaving.

27:35.755 --> 27:37.023
Go get him.

27:37.057 --> 27:38.391
- He just
pulled the [bleep] out.

27:38.458 --> 27:39.626
He's leaving.

27:39.693 --> 27:40.493
- Are you frigging kidding me?

27:40.593 --> 27:44.264
- I don't believe it.
- What do we do?

27:44.297 --> 27:45.632
- [sobbing]

27:45.699 --> 27:48.768
[engine revving]

27:54.641 --> 27:56.343
[tense music]

27:56.409 --> 27:57.477
♪ ♪

27:57.544 --> 27:59.612
- [bleep] [bleep].

27:59.679 --> 28:00.880
- Gus is back there screaming.

28:00.914 --> 28:03.550
- You have to apologize to us.
- In one hour! In one hour!

28:03.616 --> 28:06.720
- That's the whole problem.
- He wasn't here to apologize!

28:06.820 --> 28:08.822
- No job?
Are you kidding me?

28:08.855 --> 28:10.457
Look, everybody's
taking their cameras.

28:10.523 --> 28:11.524
They're all leaving.

28:11.624 --> 28:13.259
- Nobody's going to
come back in here after that.

28:13.293 --> 28:16.563
[engine revving]

28:16.629 --> 28:18.465
- [sobbing]

28:18.531 --> 28:20.834
[suspenseful music]

28:20.867 --> 28:23.103
- I don't know what happened.

28:23.169 --> 28:25.405
He wouldn't apologize to us
and he took off.

28:25.472 --> 28:28.074
And now he's gone.
- [sniffles]

28:28.108 --> 28:31.411
I don't--what do we do now?
What do we do?

28:31.478 --> 28:33.213
- [sighs]

28:33.279 --> 28:35.982
It's been emotional today.
The way that Gus acted--

28:36.082 --> 28:37.984
I mean, I've seen
that side of him.

28:38.084 --> 28:39.285
I didn't think it was going
to get that bad

28:39.352 --> 28:40.587
with Gordon being here.

28:40.653 --> 28:43.456
I mean, I'm glad it was because
he showed his true colors.

28:57.837 --> 29:00.774
[somber music]

29:00.807 --> 29:01.975
♪ ♪

29:02.008 --> 29:04.077
- Having heard
the news from my team

29:04.144 --> 29:06.646
that Gus has refused
to apologize to his staff

29:06.713 --> 29:08.581
and abandoned them,

29:08.648 --> 29:10.050
I've decided to come back

29:10.116 --> 29:14.154
and see if I can do anything
to change his mind.

29:14.187 --> 29:15.922
- Sorry, I'm a little bit too
depressed right now to cook.

29:15.989 --> 29:17.757
There would be no love
in that food.

29:17.824 --> 29:19.726
[somber music]

29:19.759 --> 29:22.529
- Oh, my god, he's here.

29:22.562 --> 29:23.329
- Oh, my goodness me.

29:23.463 --> 29:25.932
[sighs]
The producer told me Gus left.

29:25.965 --> 29:27.634
- Yeah.
- He took off.

29:27.701 --> 29:30.870
- He's obviously upset.

29:30.937 --> 29:35.342
I am prepared
to stay for all of you

29:35.408 --> 29:38.712
because I know
you need this to work.

29:38.778 --> 29:41.047
I asked Gus to do one thing,

29:41.081 --> 29:43.049
that he apologize
to the front of house.

29:43.116 --> 29:45.919
- Oh, yeah. That will never
in a million years happen.

29:45.952 --> 29:47.587
- OK, let me call him now.

29:47.654 --> 29:48.822
- Oh, lordy.

29:48.855 --> 29:50.457
- Please, Gus.
Please, Gus.

29:50.523 --> 29:51.691
[tense music]

29:51.758 --> 29:53.493
- Yeah.

29:53.560 --> 29:54.794
- Gus, it's me.

29:54.828 --> 29:56.229
- Yes, Gordon.

29:56.262 --> 29:57.697
- I'm so happy
that he came back.

29:57.764 --> 29:58.898
♪ ♪

29:58.932 --> 30:01.401
- Everybody, everybody.

30:01.468 --> 30:06.072
- I am prepared
to transform this business

30:06.106 --> 30:09.609
if you accept your mistakes
and agree to move forward

30:09.676 --> 30:11.544
with apologizing to the team.

30:11.611 --> 30:15.148
♪ ♪

30:15.215 --> 30:16.449
- And I'm willing to do that.

30:16.516 --> 30:18.118
I can be there in 15 minutes.

30:18.151 --> 30:20.220
- Bye-bye.
He's coming back.

30:20.253 --> 30:22.088
And then we are gonna
get this place

30:22.155 --> 30:23.957
back on the map where
it belongs.

30:23.990 --> 30:25.925
- Yes.
- OK?

30:25.959 --> 30:27.794
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

30:27.861 --> 30:29.095
- I appreciate you.

30:29.562 --> 30:30.630
- Come on.

30:30.697 --> 30:31.631
All right.

30:32.866 --> 30:36.269
- I'm feeling pretty relieved,
actually.

30:36.302 --> 30:39.806
I'm feeling pretty hopeful
for our future.

30:39.839 --> 30:42.809
[dramatic music]

30:42.842 --> 30:45.545
♪ ♪

30:45.578 --> 30:46.413
- Gordon.

30:46.479 --> 30:49.149
- First of all,
have you calmed down?

30:49.182 --> 30:53.386
- Yes.
- OK. Glasses off, please.

30:53.453 --> 30:57.257
I asked you
one simple thing, Gus.

30:57.323 --> 31:01.327
And that was just to apologize.

31:01.394 --> 31:04.597
I'm here to help,
but I cannot help you

31:04.664 --> 31:10.737
unless you, Gus, the boss,
is prepared to change.

31:10.770 --> 31:12.205
We've got to move forward.

31:12.272 --> 31:13.106
- That's it.

31:13.139 --> 31:15.842
- We go back in there,
apologize,

31:15.875 --> 31:17.444
but talk from the heart.

31:17.510 --> 31:18.478
- Yes.

31:18.511 --> 31:19.879
- Let's go.

31:19.946 --> 31:21.247
[low somber music]

31:21.314 --> 31:23.683
Come on.
Do the honorable thing.

31:23.750 --> 31:24.784
[Gordon sighs]

31:24.851 --> 31:26.119
- The whole staff.

31:26.186 --> 31:28.888
- The whole staff.
- OK. [sighs]

31:28.922 --> 31:30.690
I'm sorry.

31:30.757 --> 31:32.759
All right?
I'm sorry.

31:32.826 --> 31:36.262
- You makes everybody here cry.

31:36.296 --> 31:37.397
- I'm sorry.

31:37.430 --> 31:41.001
- This is last time, too,
Gus, last time.

31:41.067 --> 31:43.169
- Honey, I'm sorry
for everything I've done.

31:43.236 --> 31:45.171
[Avgi sighs and chuckles]

31:45.205 --> 31:46.973
Tabitha, I'm sorry.

31:47.007 --> 31:48.008
- I forgive you, Gus.

31:48.041 --> 31:49.776
- OK.
- We got this.

31:49.809 --> 31:51.044
[low somber music]

31:51.111 --> 31:53.913
- Honey, you know
how much I love you.

31:53.980 --> 31:55.515
I'm sorry.

31:55.582 --> 31:58.151
- At least you apologized to
us, and I accept your apology.

31:58.184 --> 31:59.786
- Yeah, we all do.

31:59.853 --> 32:01.721
[soft bright music]

32:01.755 --> 32:06.426
- First thing tomorrow morning,
we start clean, we start fresh,

32:06.493 --> 32:08.094
and we start together.

32:08.161 --> 32:09.362
Then front of house,

32:09.396 --> 32:12.198
we'll start with
a complete new organization

32:12.232 --> 32:14.334
and a setup in this dining
room to be proud of,

32:14.367 --> 32:18.238
to cook for some amazing
locals, but more importantly,

32:18.304 --> 32:21.408
starting to rebuild
this restaurant's reputation.

32:21.474 --> 32:22.709
- Thank you, Ramsay.
We appreciate it.

32:22.809 --> 32:23.843
- Yeah, thank you.
- We really do.

32:23.877 --> 32:24.878
- Yeah.

32:24.944 --> 32:26.713
- We have a lot of work to do.

32:26.780 --> 32:29.182
Ladies, front of house, let's
get everything out of here.

32:29.215 --> 32:31.017
Kitchen, Lex.
- Chef, thank you very much.

32:31.084 --> 32:32.952
- Thank you.
- Let's go.

32:33.019 --> 32:33.953
♪ ♪

32:34.020 --> 32:35.955
[Avgi sighs]

32:36.022 --> 32:38.091
♪ ♪

32:38.124 --> 32:39.259
- I thought it
was very genuine.

32:39.292 --> 32:41.094
I've never seen Gus cry.

32:41.127 --> 32:42.195
I've never seen him like that.

32:42.262 --> 32:45.699
So for him to do something
like that is very genuine.

32:45.765 --> 32:48.001
- [sobs] Don't you ever leave
us like that again, Gus.

32:48.101 --> 32:50.837
Don't you ever walk out.

32:50.904 --> 32:52.739
- I think he stays now.

32:52.806 --> 32:54.007
I believe that he stays,

32:54.074 --> 32:57.644
because it's
the last chance for Gus.

32:57.711 --> 33:00.747
[dramatic music]

33:07.053 --> 33:08.822
[upbeat jazz music]

33:08.888 --> 33:10.323
- In Cleveland, Ohio,

33:10.390 --> 33:13.493
overnight, I've had my team
come into the 4-Star Diner

33:13.560 --> 33:16.730
to give it a much-needed
refurbishment and deep clean.

33:16.763 --> 33:20.266
♪ ♪

33:20.300 --> 33:21.868
- Oh, my god.
- Wow.

33:21.901 --> 33:23.837
- Oh, it's so beautiful.

33:23.870 --> 33:25.038
- The endless knickknacks

33:25.105 --> 33:27.374
and worn-out furnishing have
been replaced.

33:27.440 --> 33:29.309
- Look at the light fixtures.

33:29.342 --> 33:31.444
- Good morning.
How beautiful is this?

33:31.444 --> 33:33.179
- Thank you, thank you,
thank you.

33:33.246 --> 33:35.015
- Lexi, let's go through
to your new kitchen.

33:35.048 --> 33:37.851
My team have given them
everything they need

33:37.884 --> 33:39.152
to bring the locals back.

33:39.185 --> 33:41.421
New fryers, a new grill,

33:41.454 --> 33:43.556
beautiful new eight-top burner
as well.

33:43.623 --> 33:44.657
- So beautiful.
- Wow.

33:44.724 --> 33:48.061
- New pots and pans,
new knives, new chinaware.

33:48.094 --> 33:49.996
- Whoo!
- Amazing.

33:50.063 --> 33:51.498
My new kitchen.
I am in love.

33:51.564 --> 33:54.901
We've got new HexClad pots
and pans, Microplane graters.

33:54.934 --> 33:56.269
We've got
a new Imperial stove.

33:56.302 --> 33:58.705
I've got a new grill,
new fryers.

33:58.738 --> 34:01.207
I'm very excited for
the dinner service tonight.

34:01.307 --> 34:03.276
I'm so ready to get back
to serving people.

34:03.343 --> 34:06.012
[suspenseful music]

34:06.046 --> 34:07.213
♪ ♪

34:07.247 --> 34:10.183
- The 135 items have gone.

34:10.216 --> 34:11.217
- Yes.
Thankfully.

34:11.284 --> 34:14.387
- Tonight,
we are cooking fresh.

34:14.420 --> 34:16.822
It's a diner,
so it's comfort food

34:16.889 --> 34:18.757
that really does
hug your soul.

34:18.824 --> 34:21.094
Firecracker shrimp, a really
nice little sharing dish.

34:21.127 --> 34:25.130
Baked feta. Just a little nod
to the Mediterranean, as well.

34:25.197 --> 34:26.933
Pork chops beautifully done.

34:26.966 --> 34:29.101
And a lovely
buffalo chicken dip.

34:29.135 --> 34:31.471
Sit down. Dig in.
Have a little taste.

34:31.538 --> 34:34.507
[upbeat music]

34:34.541 --> 34:35.942
- That's better than
canned green beans

34:35.975 --> 34:36.943
that we used to have.

34:36.976 --> 34:37.976
- Oh, wow.

34:38.011 --> 34:39.713
The new menu is amazing.

34:39.746 --> 34:42.215
We're in trouble
'cause I just started a diet

34:42.315 --> 34:44.617
and I have to behave now.

34:44.650 --> 34:46.518
- Someone's gonna have
to take this away from me.

34:46.585 --> 34:48.755
- I've also asked Gus
to come at the end of service

34:48.788 --> 34:50.556
because I want
to be able to show him that

34:50.623 --> 34:53.693
you can run the restaurant
better without him around.

34:53.760 --> 34:55.995
- When I found out that
Gus wasn't going to be here,

34:56.096 --> 34:57.263
it actually was nice.

34:57.297 --> 34:59.032
There's no tension.

34:59.099 --> 35:00.533
It feels great.

35:03.536 --> 35:06.506
♪ ♪

35:06.573 --> 35:08.675
- With the reopening
under an hour away,

35:08.708 --> 35:11.277
I brought my team in to help
with the final service,

35:11.344 --> 35:13.713
as well as give Lexi
a one-on-one

35:13.780 --> 35:16.916
to help create a five-star
meal in the 4-Star Diner.

35:16.950 --> 35:20.186
First time we met, you were
cooking an omelet on a griddle.

35:20.253 --> 35:21.721
- Yes, on a flattop.

35:21.788 --> 35:24.391
- So first off,
we don't season the eggs.

35:24.424 --> 35:26.626
If we season the eggs
too early, they'll go gray.

35:26.659 --> 35:29.329
Then from there,
just flip that up.

35:29.396 --> 35:30.730
Flip, flip, flip.

35:30.797 --> 35:32.899
So when the customers from
now on ask for an omelet,

35:32.966 --> 35:36.736
you're going to be cooking
in a pan and doing it properly.

35:36.770 --> 35:37.637
- Beautiful.

35:37.671 --> 35:39.639
- So off you go.
Make me one, please.

35:39.706 --> 35:40.774
- OK.

35:40.840 --> 35:43.043
♪ ♪

35:43.076 --> 35:44.811
- Let's go, girl.

35:44.878 --> 35:46.680
- Oh, my god.

35:46.746 --> 35:47.313
- Well?

35:47.380 --> 35:48.715
- It's delicious.

35:48.748 --> 35:50.283
- I would say I'm a
Gordon-Ramsay-trained chef now.

35:50.316 --> 35:51.718
I'm Chef Lex.

35:51.751 --> 35:54.387
I'm very excited.
Thank you so much.

35:55.055 --> 35:57.691
[suspenseful music]

35:57.724 --> 35:59.159
- How are you feeling?
- I'm feeling good.

35:59.192 --> 36:00.360
- Good.
- Feeling good.

36:00.460 --> 36:01.227
- It's not a race.
- Feeling excited to learn.

36:01.361 --> 36:02.696
- Yeah. Exactly that.
It's not a race.

36:02.762 --> 36:03.396
- No.

36:03.463 --> 36:04.397
- You good?
- Yeah.

36:04.464 --> 36:05.398
- You sure?
- Yeah.

36:05.432 --> 36:07.167
I just got that part
of it not being a race.

36:07.233 --> 36:08.335
That's what I gotta remember.

36:08.401 --> 36:09.903
- Yeah, it is definitely
not a race, OK?

36:09.936 --> 36:10.870
You know that, right?

36:11.004 --> 36:13.673
- Well, hello, hello.
Welcome to the new 4-Star.

36:13.707 --> 36:15.375
Tonight, I'm feeling
really excited,

36:15.442 --> 36:17.243
a lot different
from last night.

36:17.310 --> 36:18.878
Most of our regulars
should come back,

36:18.912 --> 36:20.680
Hopefully all of them.

36:20.714 --> 36:22.615
- [speaks Greek]
I'm happy to see you again.

36:22.682 --> 36:24.084
- You are back.
- How lovely.

36:24.150 --> 36:25.185
- Welcome back.

36:25.218 --> 36:27.320
- How is everyone?
Good?

36:27.354 --> 36:29.356
- OK, well, your food
will be over in a minute.

36:29.422 --> 36:31.324
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

36:31.358 --> 36:33.626
- All right.
Kyle, fire two feta appetizers.

36:33.660 --> 36:35.128
I'm going to fire
two potato skins.

36:35.161 --> 36:37.430
- Louder.
- Two feta appetizers.

36:37.464 --> 36:38.998
And I got
two potato skins going.

36:39.065 --> 36:40.066
- Nice.

36:40.100 --> 36:41.167
- Hi, guys.
How are you?

36:41.201 --> 36:42.202
- Hi. How are you?
- I'm good.

36:42.268 --> 36:45.638
♪ ♪

36:45.705 --> 36:47.374
- OK. Just put these
anywhere to share?

36:47.407 --> 36:48.541
- Yeah.
- OK.

36:48.608 --> 36:51.511
Without Gus here
during the service,

36:51.578 --> 36:54.514
it's just a really
positive atmosphere.

36:54.581 --> 36:55.982
- We're sharing everything.
I like it.

36:56.049 --> 36:58.485
- All right, guys,
here's a buffalo chicken dip.

36:58.518 --> 37:00.120
- How's it tasting so far?

37:00.153 --> 37:01.354
- It's terrific.
- It's good?

37:01.388 --> 37:02.222
- Very good.

37:02.288 --> 37:03.089
- I knew it would be.
[laughing] Good.

37:03.123 --> 37:04.924
- You guys been here before?
- No.

37:04.958 --> 37:07.327
- No? OK, then you don't know
the transformation,

37:07.360 --> 37:08.428
but it's beautiful.

37:08.495 --> 37:09.496
- Everybody enjoying the food?

37:09.562 --> 37:10.597
- Yeah,
they're licking it clean.

37:10.630 --> 37:14.300
[energetic percussive music]

37:14.367 --> 37:15.669
- Lex, good?

37:17.203 --> 37:19.139
- You need two pork chops.

37:19.205 --> 37:20.540
- Pork chops are working.

37:20.573 --> 37:22.108
- Pork chops shouldn't
be too much longer.

37:22.175 --> 37:24.210
- Pork chops still going to
need another minute or two.

37:24.244 --> 37:25.512
It's only at 135.

37:25.545 --> 37:27.247
- Which one?
- This one.

37:27.280 --> 37:28.381
- But what's the temp on those?

37:28.415 --> 37:30.350
- Uh-huh. OK, yeah.

37:30.417 --> 37:31.685
Learning how
to cook pork chops,

37:31.718 --> 37:33.586
you know, that's not frozen,
that's fresh,

37:33.620 --> 37:36.423
I've never cooked fresh
before, so I'm not used to it.

37:36.489 --> 37:37.557
It's also a little bit
nerve-wracking.

37:37.590 --> 37:39.659
- They're what?
- 145.

37:40.827 --> 37:42.962
- They're going to go
in the oven right now.

37:42.996 --> 37:44.631
[dramatic music]

37:46.299 --> 37:47.701
- So where are we at?

37:56.576 --> 37:57.811
- How long on pork chop?
- Uh--

37:57.844 --> 38:00.146
- We need pork chops,
like, right now.

38:00.180 --> 38:01.348
[laughter]

38:09.222 --> 38:10.557
[dramatic music]

38:10.590 --> 38:12.392
- Table five is dragging
right now.

38:12.459 --> 38:15.095
And we're dragging
on two pork chops.

38:17.063 --> 38:20.767
- All right, we need two more
pork chops, like, right now.

38:20.834 --> 38:22.736
- Pork chops shouldn't
be too much longer.

38:22.802 --> 38:25.905
- I've never cooked fresh
before, so I'm not used to it.

38:25.972 --> 38:26.973
It's crazy.

38:27.007 --> 38:30.310
- That pork chop--
is that that one for five?

38:30.343 --> 38:32.145
- Next, we are--

38:32.212 --> 38:34.347
- Then we got one pork chop on.
We've got two pork chops on.

38:34.414 --> 38:35.715
One steak, we've got two on.

38:35.749 --> 38:37.384
So we'll stay in front of that
and let it rest.

38:37.450 --> 38:38.485
- Yeah.
- Yeah? Don't worry.

38:38.551 --> 38:40.687
I'm on it. I'm on it.
Well, let's go.

38:40.787 --> 38:42.956
♪ ♪

38:42.989 --> 38:44.791
- Having Gordon Ramsay
jump in and help,

38:44.858 --> 38:46.493
it's eased my nerves
a little bit.

38:46.559 --> 38:48.461
And now I know
that we can do this.

38:48.495 --> 38:49.529
[upbeat music]

38:49.596 --> 38:50.630
Sandwiches are here.

38:50.697 --> 38:52.465
Pork chops are working.
- Great. OK.

38:52.499 --> 38:54.267
Let's get fries on there.

38:54.367 --> 38:55.669
You can go ahead
and start firing

38:55.735 --> 38:57.570
the veg for the pork chop.

38:57.637 --> 38:59.973
- Two sides of broccolini.

39:00.040 --> 39:01.241
- Love that.

39:01.307 --> 39:02.375
- There you go.

39:02.409 --> 39:03.943
- That pork chop is flying out.

39:03.977 --> 39:05.645
- There you go.
- Ooh.

39:05.712 --> 39:08.415
- Thank you.
- You are so welcome.

39:08.448 --> 39:09.516
- Lex, you good?
- Yes.

39:09.582 --> 39:11.284
- Yeah?
Not so nervous now, right?

39:11.351 --> 39:12.419
- No. Great.

39:12.485 --> 39:13.586
Loving it.
- Good, good, good.

39:13.620 --> 39:15.221
- The buffalo dip.

39:15.255 --> 39:16.456
- OK, here's our feta cheese.

39:16.489 --> 39:18.324
Your sandwiches
will be right out.

39:18.358 --> 39:20.226
- Shrimp here, guys.

39:20.260 --> 39:21.361
- Anything they're not selling?

39:21.394 --> 39:22.529
- No.
- No.

39:22.629 --> 39:23.496
If they're not,
then you just remind them.

39:23.563 --> 39:25.398
Hey, push the sandwich.
Hey, push the dip.

39:25.465 --> 39:26.499
You know what I mean, yeah?
- Yeah.

39:26.599 --> 39:28.301
I think we're gonna put a good
variety of everything.

39:28.368 --> 39:29.536
This is good for three?

39:29.602 --> 39:32.439
I feel like this experience
has changed me for the better.

39:32.505 --> 39:33.740
I feel like
it's given me a lot of tools

39:33.773 --> 39:35.709
that I didn't have before,

39:35.775 --> 39:37.544
taught me a lot of things in
the kitchen that I didn't know.

39:37.610 --> 39:41.548
I feel overall like
a more well-rounded chef.

39:41.614 --> 39:43.650
I'm very excited.
Thank you so much.

39:43.717 --> 39:47.520
[soaring orchestral music]

39:47.554 --> 39:49.456
- The sauce is very good.

39:49.522 --> 39:50.724
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

39:50.790 --> 39:51.991
- I'm very proud of our team.

39:52.058 --> 39:55.762
It's nice that she's actually
here communicating with us,

39:55.829 --> 39:56.563
helping us.

39:56.629 --> 39:58.098
It feels great.

39:58.098 --> 40:00.400
- Customers are saying that the
food is amazing, really good.

40:00.433 --> 40:01.701
I had no complaints tonight.

40:01.768 --> 40:03.470
They said they couldn't
wait to come back.

40:03.536 --> 40:05.739
Something that
we don't hear very often.

40:05.805 --> 40:08.074
- What do you think Gus is
going to think about the food?

40:09.776 --> 40:10.910
- Hi, boss.

40:11.511 --> 40:17.050
- I believe Gus cannot
recognize his own restaurant.

40:17.117 --> 40:17.817
♪ ♪

40:17.917 --> 40:20.553
I think he's proud
of all of us.

40:20.587 --> 40:22.155
- Are you happy?
- Yes, I am.

40:22.188 --> 40:23.156
- You love everything?

40:23.189 --> 40:23.957
- I love it.

40:24.124 --> 40:27.427
- I'm pretty sure
he will be a new Gus.

40:27.460 --> 40:28.561
He'll be a good guy.

40:28.595 --> 40:30.797
- And you are gonna be amazed

40:30.830 --> 40:33.867
at how smooth it runs back here
with that menu being as

40:33.933 --> 40:36.336
small as it is and everything
being as fresh as it is.

40:36.369 --> 40:37.604
I think Gus is going to

40:37.671 --> 40:38.605
fall in love with the
restaurant again,

40:38.705 --> 40:40.740
give him a passion again
for coming to work

40:40.807 --> 40:42.008
and wanting
to run the restaurant

40:42.075 --> 40:44.310
like I know he used to.

40:44.344 --> 40:46.079
- [sighs]

40:46.146 --> 40:47.280
- Right, listen.
Well done.

40:47.313 --> 40:49.382
You have been amazing.

40:49.449 --> 40:50.450
- Thank you.
- OK?

40:50.550 --> 40:52.419
- Understand the strength

40:52.485 --> 40:54.320
and the power you've got
over this diner.

40:54.387 --> 40:59.859
Let's see what Gus does next
to keep this place on track.

40:59.893 --> 41:03.196
Now I said from day one,
the problem wasn't the service.

41:03.296 --> 41:05.065
OK?
We know who the problem was.

41:05.131 --> 41:07.367
I'd like to think
we've started to sort him out.

41:07.400 --> 41:08.535
- Yes.

41:08.568 --> 41:09.502
- We're going forwards,
not backwards.

41:09.536 --> 41:10.603
all: Yes.
- Thank you so much.

41:10.637 --> 41:12.272
Oh, I am very excited
for the future.

41:12.339 --> 41:13.573
It feels good.
Everybody's happy.

41:13.606 --> 41:15.709
I'm happy, they're happy,
the cooks are happy,

41:15.742 --> 41:17.610
so yeah, I really love it.

41:17.677 --> 41:18.678
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

41:18.745 --> 41:19.512
- I'm gonna miss you guys.

41:19.612 --> 41:20.647
- And we're going
to miss you, guy.

41:20.747 --> 41:21.681
- Right. Come in here,

41:21.715 --> 41:22.816
come in here, come in here,
come in here.

41:22.882 --> 41:24.751
- I love it.
- Let's go.

41:24.784 --> 41:26.219
- I'm happy that
Gordon came in and helped us.

41:26.286 --> 41:29.155
And honestly, I'm excited
to see where we go from here.

41:29.222 --> 41:30.924
- It's so nice.
- You happy?

41:30.990 --> 41:32.225
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

41:32.258 --> 41:34.094
Look after yourself, OK?

41:34.160 --> 41:36.730
It's a new, empowered kitchen.
- Yeah.

41:36.796 --> 41:40.600
- And there's a new vibe
inside the 4-Star Diner.

41:44.704 --> 41:46.806
- You're a strong woman, OK?

41:46.873 --> 41:49.843
And you've taken a lot
and you deserve more.

41:49.876 --> 41:51.344
♪ ♪

41:51.411 --> 41:53.179
Take care, yeah?

41:53.246 --> 41:54.180
Thank you.

41:54.247 --> 41:55.648
♪ ♪

41:55.682 --> 41:58.084
[soaring orchestral music]

41:58.118 --> 42:02.255
Honestly, that was unbelievably
challenging, let me tell you.

42:02.288 --> 42:03.156
A wonderful staff.

42:03.189 --> 42:05.525
They were terrified
of their owner,

42:05.592 --> 42:07.060
working each and every day

42:07.127 --> 42:10.363
never knowing what side of Gus
they were going to encounter.

42:10.397 --> 42:11.231
After what I witnessed,

42:11.331 --> 42:13.299
I wasn't sure whether
I should help Gus.

42:13.366 --> 42:16.870
But in the end, he has
the staff that is hardworking,

42:16.936 --> 42:18.905
that are loyal,
and in love with what they do,

42:18.938 --> 42:21.841
and they're embedded
in this very community.

42:21.908 --> 42:24.077
That's the reason I stayed.

42:24.144 --> 42:26.680
Athens wasn't built in a day,
right?

42:26.713 --> 42:30.316
So let's see how Gus
does from here on in.

42:30.383 --> 42:32.152
Fingers crossed.

42:32.252 --> 42:33.653
And toes.

42:34.587 --> 42:35.655
[peaceful music]

42:35.689 --> 42:37.223
- First of all,
I want to thank

42:37.257 --> 42:40.760
Gordon Ramsay and his team
for making this possible.

42:40.860 --> 42:42.796
That remodeling looks great.

42:42.862 --> 42:45.732
Our business picked up
more than 30%.

42:45.765 --> 42:48.435
Customers love it.

42:48.501 --> 42:50.770
Our team is doing great.

42:50.837 --> 42:53.773
And I hope to see you again,
Gordon Ramsay.

42:53.840 --> 42:55.742
- Too much gravy on the lamb.

42:55.775 --> 42:57.610
- She full of [bleep].

42:57.677 --> 42:59.346
I scream, I bitch.

42:59.412 --> 43:01.481
DJ!
[bleep].

43:01.548 --> 43:02.749
Read your [bleep] ticket!

43:02.782 --> 43:04.217
- Are you delusional?

43:04.284 --> 43:05.218
- No. Are you?

43:05.285 --> 43:06.052
[bleep].

43:06.219 --> 43:08.221
Some of the customers are
just [bleep].

43:08.321 --> 43:09.622
- No, no, no!
Wow!

43:09.656 --> 43:10.957
What's she doing?
